## Group graph-index companions in Lakehouse Delete and grant warehouse CAN_USE

Context: After switching ontobricks-09x to the Serverless Starter warehouse,
Knowledge Graph builds failed with "not authorized to use this SQL Endpoint"
because the app SP had no CAN_USE on the new warehouse. Settings → Lakehouse
Delete also left adjacency/search/props companions behind: object_base() did
not strip those suffixes, so they were not in the domain purge group.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/objects.py
   object_base() uses strip_graph_leaf_suffix() so adj/search/props tables
   group with the gateway view.
2. tests/units/settings/test_delta_objects.py
   Cover suffix stripping and grouping of graph-index companions.
3. scripts/bootstrap/app-permissions.sh
   Grant CAN_USE on the app-bound SQL warehouse to both app SPs.
4. tests/units/scripts/test_app_permissions_warehouse_grant.py
   Source contract for the warehouse grant.
5. docs/deployment.md
   Document leftover companions and the warehouse CAN_USE pitfall.
6. scripts/deploy.config.sh
   Strip a leftover "#oldid" WAREHOUSE_ID export so it is not treated as a warehouse id.
7. scripts/deploy.sh
   Reject warehouse ids that start with # or are not hex.
8. Makefile
   Unset WAREHOUSE_ID before deploy so a stale shell export cannot win.

